>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `traversedata_for_ss`

``` hol4
simpLib.traversedata_for_ss : simpset -> Traverse.traverse_data
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Extracts the legacy traversal description of a simpset. Its native rewriter
is a `Traverse.REDUCER`; supplied decision procedures retain their original
representation. The result carries equality as its relation and the
simpset's traversal rules and limit.

Every ordinary simpset has this projection. Ordinary `simpLib` has no
configured subgoaler, solver list, condition-depth or term-order fields,
and needs no eligibility test or optional dispatch accessor.

Extraction does not invoke collectors, recompile installed rewrites or
reset their remaining bounded uses. The returned rewriter shares the
installed index, matchers and actual bounded controls. Subsequent traversal
construction and application retain the chosen Traverse entry point's
context lifetime: `Traverse.TRAVERSE data facts` initializes private reducer
contexts at conversion construction and reuses them on application.
The total `simpLib.SIMP_CONV` wrapper delays construction until application;
its lifetime must not be inferred from raw `TRAVERSE`.

Configured extraction is a separate extension API:
`simpExtLib.xtraversedata_for_ss` takes a `simpExtLib.simpset`, such as
`simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss`, and returns data for
`TraverseExt.XTRAVERSE`. Consumers needing only configured reducer data
use `#1 (simpExtLib.xtraversedata_for_ss ss)` on that extension set.

### Failure

Extraction does not raise a simplification failure. Constructing or
applying the returned traversal can fail as for `Traverse.TRAVERSE`.

### Example

Legacy constructor inspection needs no opt-in:

``` hol4
>>_ val data = simpLib.traversedata_for_ss simpLib.empty_ss;
>> val Traverse.REDUCER _ = hd (#rewriters data);
>> Traverse.TRAVERSE (simpLib.traversedata_for_ss bool_ss) [] “T ∧ p”;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.xtraversedata_for_ss`](#simpExtLib.xtraversedata_for_ss),
[`simpExtLib.mk_simpset`](#simpExtLib.mk_simpset).
